WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:35.400


00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:39.060
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:00:40.145 --> 00:00:43.231
HYOWON MANSION

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:54.534
Where do you live?

00:00:55.326 --> 00:00:56.870
I'll scatter 500-won coins for you!

00:00:57.495 --> 00:00:58.538
Where do you live?

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.380
A while back,
one of my students wrote a story.

00:01:07.463 --> 00:01:11.634
A girl had finally gotten a chance
to go on a date with her long-time crush,

00:01:11.718 --> 00:01:14.262
but she overslept and showed up late.

00:01:14.345 --> 00:01:15.346
I lost it reading that.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.725
I said to my student, "Hey, if it were me,
I'd have gotten up at dawn to get ready."

00:01:18.808 --> 00:01:20.185
"I wouldn't have been able to sleep."

00:01:20.268 --> 00:01:23.771
"How could she oversleep on the day
she was supposed to meet her crush?"

00:01:24.355 --> 00:01:26.357
And you know what they said?

00:01:27.066 --> 00:01:30.069
"When I feel loved,

00:01:30.153 --> 00:01:31.779
I feel at ease and sleep deeply,

00:01:32.614 --> 00:01:33.948
like I've never slept before."

00:01:36.993 --> 00:01:38.244
I slept like a baby last night.

00:02:10.818 --> 00:02:13.321
DONG-MAN: I SLEPT LIKE A BABY LAST NIGHT

00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:17.742
DONG-MAN

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.250
What are you talking about?

00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:27.585
As I said, I slept well last night.

00:02:28.336 --> 00:02:29.712
Good for you for sleeping well.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.839
I didn't sleep a wink.

00:02:32.423 --> 00:02:34.008
Why?

00:02:34.592 --> 00:02:36.719
I sent my screenplay to Eun-a,

00:02:37.845 --> 00:02:39.264
but I haven't heard back yet.

00:02:40.848 --> 00:02:41.975
I'm nervous.

00:02:42.058 --> 00:02:45.436
Is it time for your features to vanish?

00:02:46.771 --> 00:02:47.647
PRODUCER BYEON EUN-A

00:02:49.565 --> 00:02:51.693
Hey, Eun-a's calling. I have to go.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.240
Oh jeez.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.576
Hello, Eun-a.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.911
Director Lee.

00:03:03.621 --> 00:03:04.497
It's a good read.

00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:08.126
I'm so relieved.

00:03:09.293 --> 00:03:10.586
I was really worried.

00:03:12.005 --> 00:03:14.966
Eun-a, you're still at work, right?

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:16.551
Would you like to have dinner?

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.302
I already have plans tonight,

00:03:18.386 --> 00:03:20.221
so I'll email you my notes.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.697
How are you feeling these days?

00:03:39.198 --> 00:03:40.074
These days?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.118
I'm okay.

00:03:44.912 --> 00:03:47.081
Doesn't it all show up in the data anyway?

00:04:01.012 --> 00:04:02.513
Sometimes,

00:04:02.597 --> 00:04:06.934
what the data shows doesn't match
how participants say they feel.

00:04:07.018 --> 00:04:09.020
Can you tell me
how you're feeling right now?

00:04:10.438 --> 00:04:12.982
-Excuse me?
-How are you feeling right now?

00:04:13.566 --> 00:04:14.650
I feel okay.

00:04:17.111 --> 00:04:19.697
ANXIOUS

00:04:36.881 --> 00:04:37.882
Ms. Byeon Eun-a.

00:04:41.219 --> 00:04:42.220
This way, please.

00:04:43.638 --> 00:04:46.641
I wanted to tell you something.

00:04:49.018 --> 00:04:52.522
We've found another person who shares
the same "unknown" emotion pattern as you.

00:04:56.442 --> 00:04:57.568
Right here.

00:04:59.028 --> 00:05:02.073
The emotional profile matches
what you show when you get a nosebleed.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:33.020
We've only detected it once,
so we'll need to monitor it a bit more.

00:05:33.104 --> 00:05:35.940
But in any case, there's someone else.

00:05:57.628 --> 00:05:58.880
There's even an "unknown"?

00:05:59.463 --> 00:06:00.840
Apparently, there are about 20 emotions

00:06:01.549 --> 00:06:03.885
they haven't figured out what to call yet.

00:06:05.928 --> 00:06:10.016
People who exhibit the same pattern
get together to discuss

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.435
and decide what to call that emotion.

00:06:13.144 --> 00:06:14.770
That sounds like fun.

00:06:14.854 --> 00:06:16.606
I like coming up with names.

00:06:16.689 --> 00:06:18.649
I hope "unknown" shows up on mine too.

00:06:21.277 --> 00:06:24.280
When does "unknown" appear for you, Eun-a?

00:06:27.617 --> 00:06:28.951
When I get nosebleeds.

00:06:34.707 --> 00:06:36.417
When I feel overwhelming rage,

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:38.377
despair,

00:06:40.004 --> 00:06:42.048
and helplessness beyond my control.

00:06:43.382 --> 00:06:44.508
That's when I get nosebleeds.

00:06:46.427 --> 00:06:48.012
Isn't that just high blood pressure?

00:06:53.059 --> 00:06:54.810
I wonder what kind of emotion that is.

00:06:55.478 --> 00:06:56.896
What do you want to call it?

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:02.485
"Self-destructive."

00:07:13.663 --> 00:07:14.747
For some reason,

00:07:15.414 --> 00:07:17.458
that sounds scarier than "hungry."

00:07:18.501 --> 00:07:19.335
It shows "hungry" too?

00:07:20.336 --> 00:07:21.587
It sure does.

00:07:21.671 --> 00:07:23.506
But that's not even an emotion.

00:07:23.589 --> 00:07:24.590
It doesn't seem so, right?

00:07:25.299 --> 00:07:26.968
But it was the perfect word at the time.

00:07:27.593 --> 00:07:29.011
That's when I was blown away.

00:07:29.095 --> 00:07:31.222
Whoever named it "hungry"
deserves a medal.

00:07:31.305 --> 00:07:34.392
I was hurting badly, but even then,
I was very impressed.

00:07:35.017 --> 00:07:36.269
"Hungry"?

00:07:36.352 --> 00:07:37.895
What a great name for it.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:42.858
You see, I'm crazy about people
who have a way with words.

00:07:43.609 --> 00:07:45.486
My brother used to write poetry.

00:07:46.112 --> 00:07:47.780
He'd always say
there are two types of writers.

00:07:47.863 --> 00:07:51.075
Those who've read the entire dictionary
at least once and those who haven't.

00:07:51.742 --> 00:07:53.369
My brother read it three times.

00:07:53.452 --> 00:07:54.287
Wow.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.831
He eventually created his own dictionary.

00:07:57.498 --> 00:08:01.669
He was passionate about using words
to find the truth.

00:08:02.878 --> 00:08:04.130
What does he do now?

00:08:06.132 --> 00:08:07.133
Well…

00:08:07.967 --> 00:08:08.926
I guess

00:08:10.094 --> 00:08:13.180
he's welding and drinking,

00:08:14.515 --> 00:08:16.142
while still looking for the truth.

00:08:21.105 --> 00:08:23.107
A wanted poster
is better than a memorial photo.

00:08:24.483 --> 00:08:25.693
So attack, don't self-destruct.

00:08:26.485 --> 00:08:27.320
Attack.

00:08:29.196 --> 00:08:30.072
Attack.

00:08:42.001 --> 00:08:43.252
For as long as I can remember,

00:08:44.003 --> 00:08:46.088
I've never seen people as just people.

00:08:47.923 --> 00:08:49.175
I saw them as masses.

00:08:50.384 --> 00:08:51.344
Masses of emotion.

00:08:51.927 --> 00:08:54.138
Wow, I like that.

00:08:54.805 --> 00:08:55.723
"Masses of emotion."

00:08:57.516 --> 00:08:59.894
It's like a person
isn't made of flesh and blood.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:04.440
Instead, they're made from one emotion
that keeps building over a lifetime.

00:09:07.318 --> 00:09:08.861
I bet we can name everyone here

00:09:09.362 --> 00:09:11.072
after an emotion.

00:09:15.451 --> 00:09:17.078
-"Wary."
-Right.

00:09:17.578 --> 00:09:18.621
"Pretentious."

00:09:19.497 --> 00:09:20.623
"Arrogant."

00:09:26.962 --> 00:09:28.005
"Antsy."

00:09:28.756 --> 00:09:29.590
"Resentful."

00:09:30.341 --> 00:09:31.175
"Bored."

00:09:35.012 --> 00:09:36.222
They really are

00:09:37.264 --> 00:09:38.349
all masses of emotion.

00:09:38.933 --> 00:09:40.851
There aren't many good masses of emotion.

00:09:42.353 --> 00:09:43.896
I've always wondered

00:09:43.979 --> 00:09:46.899
why people on the subway look so ugly.

00:09:46.982 --> 00:09:49.235
But I guess it wasn't their faces.

00:09:49.819 --> 00:09:51.821
It was their emotions that were ugly.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.198
You know why kids are cute?

00:09:54.907 --> 00:09:56.367
Because their emotions haven't formed yet.

00:09:57.034 --> 00:09:58.119
I see.

00:09:59.245 --> 00:10:00.121
Then what about me?

00:10:00.746 --> 00:10:02.081
What kind of mass do I look like?

00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:06.460
Just say the first thing
that comes to mind.

00:10:06.544 --> 00:10:07.378
Don't change it.

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:12.967
"Anxious."

00:10:20.975 --> 00:10:21.809
You got me.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.061
I'm anxious.

00:10:25.646 --> 00:10:28.315
But isn't anxiety
just part of human nature?

00:10:29.108 --> 00:10:31.736
We exist as separate individuals,

00:10:31.819 --> 00:10:33.612
so how can we not feel anxious?

00:10:35.281 --> 00:10:37.074
My favorite word is

00:10:37.658 --> 00:10:38.617
"serenity."

00:10:39.493 --> 00:10:41.537
Calm and peaceful.

00:10:42.538 --> 00:10:44.331
I've never felt it before,

00:10:44.957 --> 00:10:47.209
but I have an idea of what it's like.

00:10:47.793 --> 00:10:49.587
It's a very safe

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.381
and very warm feeling.

00:10:54.467 --> 00:10:59.096
Like eating tangerines under a blanket
in winter, while reading comic books,

00:10:59.764 --> 00:11:01.724
but a million times better.

00:11:03.392 --> 00:11:05.144
I'm freaking talkative, you see.

00:11:05.227 --> 00:11:06.562
You know why?

00:11:06.645 --> 00:11:10.691
Whenever I feel a rush of anxiety
charging in all of a sudden,

00:11:10.775 --> 00:11:13.694
I get loud and talk my head off

00:11:13.778 --> 00:11:14.862
to chase it away.

00:11:16.322 --> 00:11:17.490
I'm afraid of silence.

00:11:18.199 --> 00:11:19.408
I'm afraid

00:11:20.117 --> 00:11:21.994
the truth might pop out of nowhere
in the silence.

00:11:22.953 --> 00:11:23.787
Like boom.

00:11:27.583 --> 00:11:29.168
What kind of truth?

00:11:39.303 --> 00:11:40.763
When it's quiet…

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.685
I feel like a Gollum-like demon
will appear…

00:11:49.104 --> 00:11:50.856
and whisper in my ear.

00:11:53.275 --> 00:11:54.109
You…

00:11:54.944 --> 00:11:57.029
are worthless.

00:12:01.534 --> 00:12:02.409
"You…

00:12:04.537 --> 00:12:05.829
are worthless."

00:12:59.216 --> 00:13:01.010
I don't usually watch

00:13:01.802 --> 00:13:02.970
my own films.

00:13:05.014 --> 00:13:06.974
Maybe "I can't" would be more accurate.

00:13:07.057 --> 00:13:08.559
Because I think I did it all wrong.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:13.897
But this time,
the original novel was so good

00:13:13.981 --> 00:13:15.608
that there was no way to get it wrong.

00:13:17.651 --> 00:13:21.739
I thought, "I've finally made a film
my daughter would be proud of."

00:13:25.534 --> 00:13:26.535
Q&amp;A SCREENING

00:13:26.619 --> 00:13:28.829
Before being her mom,
as an experienced actress,

00:13:29.622 --> 00:13:31.832
I've always had that kind of thirst.

00:13:38.756 --> 00:13:40.758
Mr. Choi invited us for drinks at Agit.

00:13:40.841 --> 00:13:42.217
He says it's his treat.

00:13:42.301 --> 00:13:44.303
The man is just ecstatic.

00:13:44.386 --> 00:13:46.013
We hit a million in record time,

00:13:46.096 --> 00:13:48.307
and now, he's already excited
about hitting ten million.

00:13:49.933 --> 00:13:50.893
You're coming, right?

00:13:52.394 --> 00:13:55.522
I have plans at this restaurant
I waited two months to get into.

00:13:55.606 --> 00:13:58.609
I didn't think you were the type
to wait like that, Mi-ran.

00:13:59.234 --> 00:14:00.903
I'm serious when it comes to food.

00:14:02.988 --> 00:14:05.240
Why don't we go for a drink?
Mr. Choi will be waiting.

00:14:05.324 --> 00:14:07.660
Don't say you're "serious"
about something.

00:14:08.744 --> 00:14:10.496
Just say, "I like food."

00:14:10.579 --> 00:14:12.373
That sounds much more genuine.

00:14:14.083 --> 00:14:18.253
Using trendy phrases
and trying to be "hip," as you call it,

00:14:18.879 --> 00:14:20.047
isn't hip at all.

00:14:21.382 --> 00:14:24.593
Politicians and actors
who lack their own style of expression

00:14:25.177 --> 00:14:26.220
never last long.

00:14:28.514 --> 00:14:30.224
-Let's have drinks some other time.
-Yes, ma'am.

00:14:40.359 --> 00:14:42.111
-I'll see you at home.
-Take care.

00:14:56.041 --> 00:14:57.793
-Good job.
-Nice work, everyone.

00:14:58.669 --> 00:15:00.379
Stop looking at your phone.

00:15:01.005 --> 00:15:01.922
Are you that happy?

00:15:03.799 --> 00:15:06.260
You can almost smell success
in the numbers.

00:15:07.344 --> 00:15:08.762
Check out the advance ticket sales.

00:15:08.846 --> 00:15:10.347
MY MOTHER
ADVANCE TICKET SALES: 65.8%

00:15:10.431 --> 00:15:12.641
It's been so long
since I've seen numbers like this.

00:15:13.267 --> 00:15:14.101
All right.

00:15:14.852 --> 00:15:18.105
The mom stepped in to fix
what her daughter botched up.

00:15:18.731 --> 00:15:20.357
Sorry for botching things up.

00:15:20.441 --> 00:15:21.775
Come on, that's how it is.

00:15:21.859 --> 00:15:24.278
You tank ten before you land one.

00:15:24.361 --> 00:15:25.195
You know this.

00:15:25.279 --> 00:15:27.031
I wonder when I'll finally land that one.

00:15:28.073 --> 00:15:29.700
Just stay right by my side.

00:15:29.783 --> 00:15:31.869
As long as you're with me,
you'll land at least one.

00:15:32.661 --> 00:15:33.829
We're doing this.

00:15:34.496 --> 00:15:36.498
Here's to hitting ten million!

00:15:36.582 --> 00:15:37.416
Let's go!

00:15:37.499 --> 00:15:39.251
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.965
What's Director Park Gyeong-se doing?

00:15:45.049 --> 00:15:46.508
Tell him to come for a drink.

00:15:46.592 --> 00:15:48.844
Just leave him alone.
He's not in a good place these days.

00:15:48.927 --> 00:15:50.763
DECISION TO STAY

00:17:19.434 --> 00:17:21.728
Get some rest on your days off!

00:17:21.812 --> 00:17:23.313
Don't just drink!

00:17:51.592 --> 00:17:52.968
THE EIGHT CLUB

00:17:54.052 --> 00:17:55.554
Read this, Hwang Dong-man.

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:58.515
We live in an era
where people leave comments

00:17:58.599 --> 00:18:01.727
like mutts leaving crap wherever they go.

00:18:02.519 --> 00:18:05.439
We see your crap every single day.

00:18:05.522 --> 00:18:08.525
Our group chat is filled with your crap.

00:18:09.109 --> 00:18:11.528
You're supposed to clean up
your own crap, you know.

00:18:12.112 --> 00:18:16.742
Whenever I think of you,
I feel nothing but rage all day

00:18:16.825 --> 00:18:21.038
because of all the crap
you've written and said so far.

00:18:22.039 --> 00:18:25.125
Every day, I think about the things
I didn't get to say to you that day.

00:18:26.126 --> 00:18:27.753
"I should've said that."

00:18:27.836 --> 00:18:29.338
"I should've said that too."

00:18:29.421 --> 00:18:31.590
After a sleepless, rage-filled night,

00:18:31.673 --> 00:18:35.260
I've decided to sit down
and organize my thoughts clearly.

00:18:36.762 --> 00:18:38.722
I want you to read this out loud

00:18:39.431 --> 00:18:41.600
the same way I did.

00:18:41.683 --> 00:18:43.644
I want you to swallow these words

00:18:44.269 --> 00:18:46.021
the same way I did.

00:18:46.688 --> 00:18:47.731
And I hope it hurts.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.858
I hope it hurts

00:18:49.942 --> 00:18:52.778
when you read this and choke it down.

00:18:52.861 --> 00:18:54.279
No vegetables today?

00:18:58.283 --> 00:18:59.117
One.

00:18:59.993 --> 00:19:02.955
When the whole country
raved about Ki-ri's drama,

00:19:03.038 --> 00:19:05.332
you refused to watch it
even though he's your friend.

00:19:05.415 --> 00:19:06.750
Then you said,

00:19:06.833 --> 00:19:10.128
"For some reason,
I'm not into things everyone else likes."

00:19:10.212 --> 00:19:11.546
"This is why I haven't made it yet."

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:12.756
"I'm just too niche."

00:19:12.839 --> 00:19:14.424
This is why I haven't made it yet.

00:19:14.508 --> 00:19:15.467
I'm just too niche.

00:19:17.094 --> 00:19:19.263
Do you remember the vibe in the room
when you said that?

00:19:19.972 --> 00:19:21.848
Everyone went quiet.

00:19:22.849 --> 00:19:24.768
Why do you think we stopped talking?

00:19:25.394 --> 00:19:27.729
Because we were pissed off.

00:19:28.647 --> 00:19:30.232
You know why you're not successful.

00:19:30.315 --> 00:19:32.651
I know. We all know.

00:19:33.193 --> 00:19:36.196
But seeing you
try to one-up whoever's in front of you

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:38.615
just freaking pissed us off.

00:19:38.699 --> 00:19:41.243
Want me to run through
all the masters of niche cinema?

00:19:41.326 --> 00:19:44.329
Or how about a list
of successful niche film directors?

00:19:44.413 --> 00:19:46.665
Being niche isn't why you haven't made it.

00:19:47.291 --> 00:19:48.959
You just have no talent.

00:19:49.042 --> 00:19:50.252
Your work is boring!

00:19:58.218 --> 00:19:59.511
Damn it!

00:20:07.519 --> 00:20:09.771
I WANT YOU TO READ THIS OUT LOUD,
THE SAME WAY I DID…

00:20:16.528 --> 00:20:18.572
He really went there, didn't he?

00:20:18.655 --> 00:20:19.531
No way.

00:20:20.741 --> 00:20:23.493
I bet Hwang Dong-man
wants to die right now.

00:20:23.577 --> 00:20:24.578
What is it?

00:20:27.414 --> 00:20:28.332
No way.

00:20:39.634 --> 00:20:41.178
They look real.

00:20:41.261 --> 00:20:42.637
It has an amazing grip.

00:20:43.764 --> 00:20:45.349
It's just like a real gun.

00:20:49.686 --> 00:20:51.188
What's the movie about?

00:20:52.064 --> 00:20:55.901
Public officials who take care of people
who stress out citizens.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:59.863
Sounds like a lot of politicians
will get killed.

00:21:05.285 --> 00:21:07.162
Click, clack.

00:21:08.205 --> 00:21:09.247
Bang!

00:21:10.415 --> 00:21:13.543
This only has two loading steps,
so it doesn't sound as good.

00:21:14.586 --> 00:21:17.339
If you're going to kill someone,
you might as well use something cathartic.

00:21:18.882 --> 00:21:21.301
Click, click, clack, thunk!

00:21:21.385 --> 00:21:22.803
Bang!

00:21:23.387 --> 00:21:25.639
You need at least four loading steps

00:21:25.722 --> 00:21:29.351
to boost the action
and make the audience's hearts pound.

00:21:29.434 --> 00:21:31.436
Can't we use real guns?

00:21:32.354 --> 00:21:34.856
We can, but it's a headache.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:38.443
The firearms supplier drops them off
at the police station on filming day.

00:21:38.527 --> 00:21:41.279
The production company has to pick them up

00:21:41.363 --> 00:21:43.698
and then return them exactly on time,

00:21:43.782 --> 00:21:45.200
so it's better not to use them.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:48.995
Come on, these look and feel
just like real guns!

00:21:51.623 --> 00:21:54.042
See? You tried to dodge it.

00:21:57.671 --> 00:21:58.672
Amazing, right?

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:29.953
Two.

00:22:31.955 --> 00:22:36.751
On the FAM tour, you had the nerve
to ask a famous director for their name.

00:22:37.502 --> 00:22:39.462
The way you pretended not to know someone

00:22:39.546 --> 00:22:42.757
who clearly had no reason to know you
was sheer arrogance.

00:22:42.841 --> 00:22:44.801
Everyone else just stayed quiet
the whole trip,

00:22:44.885 --> 00:22:47.971
but you couldn't stop talking
because you were busy hiding

00:22:48.054 --> 00:22:49.931
the fact that you were a nobody!

00:22:50.015 --> 00:22:54.603
You talked your head off
like your life depended on it!

00:22:55.979 --> 00:22:59.107
In the end, you proved to everyone
that you were a nobody!

00:22:59.191 --> 00:23:02.110
That's why we never
go on FAM tours with you anymore.

00:23:05.155 --> 00:23:06.698
Because there's no reason

00:23:08.283 --> 00:23:10.911
to put up with your crap in public.

00:23:13.955 --> 00:23:14.915
Three.

00:23:15.832 --> 00:23:19.502
You keep getting rejected,
but you do it again

00:23:20.086 --> 00:23:21.713
-and again.
-Mr. Hwang Dong-man?

00:23:21.796 --> 00:23:22.631
Yes?

00:23:27.969 --> 00:23:29.012
Back to three.

00:23:30.305 --> 00:23:33.308
You keep getting rejected,
but you do it again

00:23:34.267 --> 00:23:35.101
and again.

00:23:35.769 --> 00:23:37.646
You refuse to give up.

00:23:37.729 --> 00:23:39.439
Now it makes me wonder,

00:23:41.107 --> 00:23:43.235
"Maybe he's hoping he can keep doing this

00:23:44.152 --> 00:23:45.654
until the day he dies."

00:23:53.912 --> 00:23:55.830
Hello, it's good to see you here.

00:24:06.091 --> 00:24:08.009
Hwang Dong-man, did you read it?

00:24:10.512 --> 00:24:12.013
I know you can hear me!

00:24:16.309 --> 00:24:17.727
Read it out loud!

00:24:18.228 --> 00:24:21.314
Choke down every single word, all right?

00:24:23.191 --> 00:24:25.277
That dumbass can't even act.

00:24:26.027 --> 00:24:27.445
Come on, that's enough.

00:24:33.785 --> 00:24:34.995
What's wrong?

00:24:35.078 --> 00:24:36.913
Hwang Dong-man just walked by.

00:24:36.997 --> 00:24:37.914
Really?

00:24:40.166 --> 00:24:41.501
That bastard didn't even read it.

00:24:43.003 --> 00:24:44.170
I guarantee it.

00:24:45.255 --> 00:24:46.423
But the unread count is zero.

00:24:46.506 --> 00:24:48.425
He just cleared the count
but didn't actually read it.

00:24:49.217 --> 00:24:51.761
What's the root of all mental illnesses?

00:24:52.387 --> 00:24:53.513
Refusing to face reality.

00:24:53.596 --> 00:24:55.181
It'd kill him if he read it.

00:24:55.265 --> 00:24:56.433
He won't read it.

00:24:56.516 --> 00:24:57.475
He can't!

00:24:57.976 --> 00:24:59.394
He's always been like that.

00:24:59.477 --> 00:25:01.271
Whenever anyone hits him with the truth,

00:25:03.440 --> 00:25:04.316
he doesn't listen.

00:25:04.399 --> 00:25:06.526
It's meant to hurt him like hell,

00:25:06.609 --> 00:25:09.362
but the idiot just laughs
and rambles about something else.

00:25:09.446 --> 00:25:10.989
Gyeong-se,

00:25:11.072 --> 00:25:12.741
you took a crap in the group chat too.

00:25:12.824 --> 00:25:14.284
I know I did!

00:25:14.868 --> 00:25:17.746
I wanted to show him
he's not the only one who can take a crap.

00:25:17.829 --> 00:25:20.874
Jun-hwan says he'll get better
after wearing the emotion watch.

00:25:20.957 --> 00:25:24.169
Tell that asshole to take some damn meds
instead of wearing that stupid watch!

00:25:33.136 --> 00:25:34.346
What just happened?

00:25:46.733 --> 00:25:48.276
Damn it!

00:25:49.944 --> 00:25:51.363
Are you kidding me?

00:25:51.446 --> 00:25:53.323
-Hey, Gyeong-se!
-That little…

00:25:53.406 --> 00:25:54.741
Where are you going?

00:25:55.367 --> 00:25:56.326
Damn it.

00:26:40.120 --> 00:26:41.413
I can't even finish reading it.

00:26:44.374 --> 00:26:46.376
There's something I didn't tell you.

00:26:49.712 --> 00:26:50.922
If you scroll up,

00:26:52.340 --> 00:26:55.510
you'll see all the crap
that bastard wrote about me.

00:26:55.593 --> 00:26:56.428
Why do you think I--

00:26:56.511 --> 00:26:57.804
Cham, cham, cham.

00:27:02.058 --> 00:27:04.310
Why do you think
I was so harsh on Dong-man

00:27:04.394 --> 00:27:05.603
and banned him from here?

00:27:06.312 --> 00:27:08.273
Because I couldn't stand him?

00:27:08.857 --> 00:27:12.444
It's because I'm embarrassed
by how you lose your shit around him!

00:27:13.236 --> 00:27:15.405
One word from him,
and you shake with rage!

00:27:16.364 --> 00:27:17.991
Aren't you ashamed to face your juniors?

00:27:18.741 --> 00:27:20.452
What about our staff?

00:27:21.619 --> 00:27:23.163
If you do this one more time,

00:27:23.246 --> 00:27:24.747
I'll take down
the "Hwang Dong-man not allowed" sign

00:27:24.831 --> 00:27:27.083
and put up one that says
"Park Gyeong-se not allowed."

00:27:33.339 --> 00:27:34.257
Damn it.

00:27:44.267 --> 00:27:46.311
I think we'll hit ten million
in record time.

00:27:49.397 --> 00:27:52.650
I can probably quit right now
and live off this for the rest of my life.

00:27:52.734 --> 00:27:54.068
But you know how it is.

00:27:54.152 --> 00:27:55.278
I'll just use that money for a new film.

00:27:58.990 --> 00:28:00.366
Excuse me, sir.

00:28:00.450 --> 00:28:02.243
Something weird just came up.

00:28:03.328 --> 00:28:05.079
I think you should see this.

00:28:05.163 --> 00:28:07.665
Hey, I'll call you back later.

00:28:07.749 --> 00:28:08.750
Okay.

00:28:11.002 --> 00:28:12.045
Something weird?

00:28:13.213 --> 00:28:14.172
What is it?

00:28:19.302 --> 00:28:22.138
"It bothers me
to see her with Jang Mi-ran…"

00:28:32.273 --> 00:28:34.901
IT BOTHERS ME TO SEE HER WITH JANG MI-RAN,
ACTING LIKE A LOVING MOTHER AND DAUGHTER

00:28:34.984 --> 00:28:36.069
WHEN THEY AREN'T EVEN RELATED

00:28:39.197 --> 00:28:40.281
When was this posted?

00:28:42.867 --> 00:28:43.785
Huh?

00:28:43.868 --> 00:28:45.161
It's me.

00:28:45.245 --> 00:28:46.329
Did you see the social media post?

00:28:48.581 --> 00:28:49.582
What is it?

00:28:59.259 --> 00:29:01.344
"It bothers me
to see her with Jang Mi-ran,

00:29:01.427 --> 00:29:04.180
acting like a loving mother and daughter

00:29:05.181 --> 00:29:06.432
when they aren't even related."

00:29:07.725 --> 00:29:09.394
"I still remember that girl

00:29:09.477 --> 00:29:11.479
from elementary school 23 years ago."

00:29:12.272 --> 00:29:14.274
"Last name Byeon.'"

00:29:16.943 --> 00:29:18.528
"She's Oh Jeong-hui's daughter,

00:29:18.611 --> 00:29:20.572
but she was neglected and grew up

00:29:21.239 --> 00:29:22.866
without her parents."

00:29:25.243 --> 00:29:27.745
"Oh Jeong-hui
was an unknown actor back then,

00:29:27.829 --> 00:29:31.708
but she looked too elegant
to live in our shabby neighborhood."

00:29:31.791 --> 00:29:33.668
"That's why I remember her name."

00:29:35.587 --> 00:29:38.756
"Compared to Oh Jeong-hui,
her daughter was quiet and ordinary."

00:29:39.632 --> 00:29:42.927
"I didn't think much of it at the time,
but looking back now,

00:29:43.011 --> 00:29:45.013
my heart simply goes out to her."

00:29:46.264 --> 00:29:48.433
"I wonder what she's doing now

00:29:49.642 --> 00:29:51.561
and how her life is going."

00:29:52.812 --> 00:29:54.647
Just stop, will you?

00:29:54.731 --> 00:29:56.983
You're not fed up with the film industry
that's starving your family,

00:29:57.066 --> 00:29:58.776
but you're fed up with me?

00:29:58.860 --> 00:30:01.696
You miss that hellhole so much?

00:30:03.281 --> 00:30:05.074
One day, my dad left.

00:30:10.288 --> 00:30:11.831
Then, my mom left.

00:30:16.961 --> 00:30:19.130
I went to school like nothing happened,

00:30:20.506 --> 00:30:24.177
even though my heart was pounding so hard,
I thought it'd pop out of my chest.

00:30:25.470 --> 00:30:27.305
I went to school like nothing happened,

00:30:28.264 --> 00:30:29.349
ate alone…

00:30:31.392 --> 00:30:32.435
and slept alone.

00:30:37.106 --> 00:30:38.900
Why didn't you tell anyone?

00:30:40.360 --> 00:30:43.112
You could've told your teacher
that you were alone.

00:30:48.493 --> 00:30:50.078
Did you think it might put you in danger?

00:30:51.955 --> 00:30:52.872
No.

00:30:56.417 --> 00:30:58.419
I couldn't let anyone find out
I'd been abandoned.

00:31:16.229 --> 00:31:18.439
One word from the daughter,
and it'll be over.

00:31:18.523 --> 00:31:20.441
"It's not true. I was never neglected."

00:31:20.525 --> 00:31:23.695
Why go overboard
and issue an official statement?

00:31:24.737 --> 00:31:28.199
People know Oh Jeong-hui
got divorced at a young age.

00:31:28.282 --> 00:31:30.910
Her husband raised their kid.
She wasn't neglected.

00:31:30.994 --> 00:31:32.203
That's her side of the story.

00:31:32.286 --> 00:31:33.579
The truth doesn't matter right now.

00:31:33.663 --> 00:31:36.124
What matters
is making it look like the truth!

00:31:36.207 --> 00:31:39.669
It'll only look like the truth
if the daughter says it herself.

00:31:39.752 --> 00:31:42.422
Oh Jeong-hui can talk all she wants,
but no one will believe her.

00:31:42.505 --> 00:31:45.842
How can she ask her daughter
if she can't get in touch with her?

00:31:46.592 --> 00:31:48.636
What do you mean
she can't get in touch with her?

00:31:49.470 --> 00:31:52.890
You know this is a bad sign, right?

00:31:52.974 --> 00:31:55.560
Never mind My Mother tanking
right before hitting ten million.

00:31:55.643 --> 00:32:00.023
One wrong move and Oh Jeong-hui
can kiss her career goodbye.

00:32:02.650 --> 00:32:04.360
Okay, fine. Go ahead.

00:32:04.444 --> 00:32:06.320
Issue an official statement for now.

00:32:08.239 --> 00:32:09.449
But make it sound really sad.

00:32:09.532 --> 00:32:11.743
No, heartbreaking. You know what I mean.

00:32:11.826 --> 00:32:13.369
"I worried about her my whole life."

00:32:13.453 --> 00:32:14.704
"We got divorced when she was little,

00:32:14.787 --> 00:32:17.123
but I did the best I could
while raising her."

00:32:17.206 --> 00:32:19.667
Write something along those lines,
and show it to her.

00:32:19.751 --> 00:32:23.212
Ask her if it's okay
to issue such a statement.

00:32:23.838 --> 00:32:26.382
She'll know whether it's okay or not.

00:32:29.010 --> 00:32:30.762
If you issue it without thinking,

00:32:30.845 --> 00:32:32.722
and the daughter comes forward
claiming she was neglected,

00:32:32.805 --> 00:32:34.640
Oh Jeong-hui's career will be over.

00:32:34.724 --> 00:32:35.975
So just ask her, damn it!

00:32:41.522 --> 00:32:42.607
And one more thing, Mr. Park.

00:32:43.900 --> 00:32:45.193
Find the daughter.

00:32:46.110 --> 00:32:47.653
Find her!

00:32:47.737 --> 00:32:50.406
We need to find her and fix this,

00:32:50.490 --> 00:32:52.283
even if it means making amends or begging!

00:32:56.370 --> 00:32:58.498
DM the person who posted it.

00:32:58.581 --> 00:33:02.210
Tell them to take it down, or we'll sue
for spreading false information.

00:33:02.293 --> 00:33:03.336
Intimidate them a bit.

00:33:03.419 --> 00:33:04.670
-Got it?
-Yes, sir.

00:33:05.713 --> 00:33:06.589
Damn it!

00:33:22.271 --> 00:33:23.773
She left her husband and child,

00:33:25.399 --> 00:33:27.944
who weren't good enough for her…

00:33:30.279 --> 00:33:33.741
and replaced them
with a shiny new husband and child.

00:33:36.744 --> 00:33:39.288
There really are people
who get everything they want.

00:33:53.678 --> 00:33:56.389
When depression pressed down on me
like a heavy iron weight,

00:33:56.472 --> 00:33:58.266
and I couldn't even sit up,

00:33:59.183 --> 00:34:00.518
all I wanted…

00:34:01.561 --> 00:34:02.728
was weather.

00:34:04.438 --> 00:34:06.274
If it were a warm, spring day…

00:34:07.358 --> 00:34:09.110
If cherry blossoms were in the air…

00:34:10.444 --> 00:34:14.699
I'd read Park Gyeong-se's message
as if it were a love letter.

00:34:56.532 --> 00:34:57.366
"Don't take this…"

00:34:57.450 --> 00:35:02.371
Don't take this as me trying to tell you
to get your act together.

00:35:03.206 --> 00:35:06.792
At this point,
I'd feel even more bitter and resentful

00:35:06.876 --> 00:35:09.086
if I thought
you'd finally gotten your life together.

00:35:10.546 --> 00:35:14.425
I think the only way
I could die in peace is to know

00:35:15.009 --> 00:35:16.636
you're still exactly where you are
right now.

00:35:17.595 --> 00:35:23.434
So please keep living the way
you always have until the very end.

00:35:25.102 --> 00:35:28.981
"Keep living the way you always have
until the very end."

00:35:30.274 --> 00:35:31.192
Seven.

00:35:32.151 --> 00:35:33.110
Goddamn it.

00:35:33.778 --> 00:35:35.321
Why the hell is it so long?

00:35:35.821 --> 00:35:38.491
He talked about dying,
so this should be the end.

00:35:46.165 --> 00:35:48.376
A SCARY WOMAN
BY LEE JUN-HWAN

00:35:49.710 --> 00:35:50.586
You know,

00:35:51.712 --> 00:35:54.882
I believed you when you said
you'd really go mainstream this time.

00:35:55.633 --> 00:35:56.801
When I read the first draft,

00:35:57.551 --> 00:36:00.221
I thought,
"He worked really hard on this."

00:36:00.846 --> 00:36:03.891
"A bit more effort
would definitely make it mainstream."

00:36:05.101 --> 00:36:11.190
So tell me why I'm seeing your signature
B-movie vibes in the revised draft.

00:36:12.108 --> 00:36:13.317
One thing's for sure.

00:36:14.485 --> 00:36:16.487
You think there's an actor

00:36:17.071 --> 00:36:17.947
who'd do this?

00:36:18.030 --> 00:36:20.116
No, not among A-listers.

00:36:20.741 --> 00:36:23.244
Are you going to make another film
with a B-lister

00:36:23.327 --> 00:36:24.954
and take pride in simply having made it?

00:36:25.037 --> 00:36:27.039
You said you wouldn't do that anymore.

00:36:27.123 --> 00:36:30.376
That's what you promised me
when you signed the contract.

00:36:30.459 --> 00:36:33.462
You might feel this way
because the character stands out,

00:36:34.505 --> 00:36:36.048
but it doesn't have B-movie vibes.

00:36:36.841 --> 00:36:39.218
Even Eun-a said the revised draft
was much better.

00:36:45.558 --> 00:36:48.102
So if Byeon Eun-a likes it,
does it mean it's good?

00:36:49.437 --> 00:36:52.106
Why do you all keep saying,
"But Byeon Eun-a liked it"?

00:36:52.189 --> 00:36:53.274
Is she always right?

00:36:53.357 --> 00:36:55.234
You keep singing praises about her.

00:36:55.318 --> 00:36:57.194
Haven't you guys on the second floor heard

00:36:58.112 --> 00:37:00.114
I've been giving her a freaking hard time?

00:37:00.823 --> 00:37:02.158
You want to get kicked out of your office?

00:37:02.658 --> 00:37:05.077
Eun-a reads screenplays objectively

00:37:05.161 --> 00:37:06.537
without picturing specific actors.

00:37:06.620 --> 00:37:09.081
You have to read them
with specific actors in mind!

00:37:09.915 --> 00:37:10.791
It makes sense now.

00:37:12.043 --> 00:37:14.962
I was so frustrated reading this
because I couldn't imagine the cast.

00:37:20.843 --> 00:37:21.719
Ax, get in here.

00:37:25.556 --> 00:37:28.017
Ax, my ass. She can't even hit the mark.

00:37:29.560 --> 00:37:30.394
I said get in here!

00:37:42.573 --> 00:37:44.241
I heard you said this was good.

00:37:45.534 --> 00:37:47.286
Who should we cast for this?

00:37:47.370 --> 00:37:48.829
Give me some names.

00:37:55.044 --> 00:37:56.295
Come on.

00:37:57.421 --> 00:37:58.297
Jang Mi-ran.

00:37:58.381 --> 00:38:00.841
Why would she agree to this
unless she wants to end her career?

00:38:01.759 --> 00:38:03.511
Will you cast her yourself?

00:38:04.678 --> 00:38:07.181
You need to think about the casting
when you read.

00:38:07.264 --> 00:38:09.100
If you like it, that's all?

00:38:09.183 --> 00:38:10.518
Are we publishing this as a book?

00:38:10.601 --> 00:38:11.852
Are we a publisher now?

00:38:12.561 --> 00:38:14.897
How frustrating.

00:38:25.783 --> 00:38:27.993
I'm sorry.
I should've persuaded him better.

00:38:29.286 --> 00:38:30.413
It's okay.

00:38:32.415 --> 00:38:33.958
I agree that the revised draft is better.

00:38:35.835 --> 00:38:37.962
If we can't trust our own instincts,
who can we trust?

00:38:51.142 --> 00:38:53.269
Hwang Dong-man has been messaging you.

00:38:56.605 --> 00:38:58.649
You two must be getting close.

00:38:58.732 --> 00:39:01.610
What, are you really going to see
for yourself what he's like?

00:39:04.655 --> 00:39:05.865
Aren't you embarrassed by him?

00:39:15.666 --> 00:39:17.626
I'm more embarrassed for you,
saying something like that.

00:39:30.723 --> 00:39:31.724
I just wish

00:39:33.476 --> 00:39:36.103
you'd give up and leave the film industry.

00:39:37.480 --> 00:39:41.066
Don't kid yourself into thinking
that you're actually talented

00:39:41.692 --> 00:39:44.445
just because you shone briefly.

00:39:45.112 --> 00:39:48.407
Or else you'll end up like Hwang Dong-man
with 20 years down the drain.

00:40:11.805 --> 00:40:12.848
Delivery!

00:40:25.736 --> 00:40:26.820
That'll be 28,000 won.

00:40:28.072 --> 00:40:29.240
Food's here.

00:40:36.914 --> 00:40:38.123
I said the food's here.

00:40:48.842 --> 00:40:49.677
Hey.

00:40:59.019 --> 00:41:00.938
-How much?
-It's 28,000 won.

00:41:07.403 --> 00:41:08.487
-Enjoy your food.
-Thank you.

00:42:22.811 --> 00:42:23.812
MS. BYEON EUN-A

00:42:27.983 --> 00:42:29.526
What made you call me at this hour?

00:42:32.237 --> 00:42:33.906
Tell me a funny story.

00:42:36.659 --> 00:42:37.534
Do you have

00:42:38.160 --> 00:42:39.161
a sixth sense?

00:42:39.787 --> 00:42:40.871
How did you know to call?

00:42:41.997 --> 00:42:44.667
I had a really weird experience just now.

00:42:45.334 --> 00:42:47.503
I ordered delivery and was lying down,

00:42:47.586 --> 00:42:48.712
but I didn't fall asleep.

00:42:48.796 --> 00:42:51.006
I could hear my brother moving around.

00:42:51.632 --> 00:42:52.758
Then suddenly,

00:42:53.509 --> 00:42:56.220
my brother got on top of my back

00:42:56.303 --> 00:42:59.098
and started stomping on me.

00:42:59.181 --> 00:43:00.933
I thought he had lost his mind.

00:43:01.016 --> 00:43:03.310
I was sleepy and annoyed,

00:43:03.394 --> 00:43:04.728
but too lazy to get up.

00:43:05.562 --> 00:43:06.438
But then

00:43:07.231 --> 00:43:10.025
I heard him grab a bottle of alcohol
from across the room.

00:43:17.950 --> 00:43:20.828
So I thought,
"Then who's on my back right now?"

00:43:22.454 --> 00:43:23.372
It's sleep paralysis.

00:43:23.956 --> 00:43:27.042
That's when I thought I might die,

00:43:27.126 --> 00:43:29.294
but I couldn't even move a finger.

00:43:29.378 --> 00:43:30.546
You know how it is.

00:43:30.629 --> 00:43:32.631
You can't move an inch,
no matter how hard you try.

00:43:33.632 --> 00:43:37.219
This bastard was dancing on my back,
and I'm losing my mind.

00:43:38.262 --> 00:43:39.096
Just then…

00:43:40.514 --> 00:43:41.598
Delivery!

00:43:42.516 --> 00:43:43.559
I thought, "Yes, I'm saved!"

00:43:44.435 --> 00:43:45.519
Food's here.

00:43:45.602 --> 00:43:47.646
"Please kick me."

00:43:47.730 --> 00:43:49.148
I said the food's here.

00:43:49.231 --> 00:43:51.483
"Come on, just kick me!"

00:43:51.567 --> 00:43:52.818
"As hard as you can!"

00:43:54.069 --> 00:43:56.113
"Yes, that's right."

00:43:56.196 --> 00:43:57.030
"Come on."

00:43:58.532 --> 00:44:00.367
-Hey.
-"Just kick me, you bastard!"

00:44:00.451 --> 00:44:01.785
"Please!"

00:44:05.914 --> 00:44:07.708
-"Damn it."
-It's 28,000 won.

00:44:10.169 --> 00:44:12.171
I felt like I was dying,

00:44:12.254 --> 00:44:14.298
but he just kept drinking.

00:44:14.381 --> 00:44:16.842
It made me feel sad all of a sudden.

00:44:16.925 --> 00:44:19.762
"I've got enough people to fight,
and now I have to fight sleep paralysis?"

00:44:20.888 --> 00:44:23.098
"Forget it. I'm not going to fight it."

00:44:23.182 --> 00:44:25.809
"Go ahead and beat me, sleep paralysis."

00:44:25.893 --> 00:44:27.352
"It's not like I'm going to die."

00:44:28.228 --> 00:44:29.188
You know what I mean.

00:44:29.271 --> 00:44:32.691
It feels like you're going to die,
but you don't actually die.

00:44:33.442 --> 00:44:35.903
"So go ahead, sleep paralysis. You win."

00:44:37.070 --> 00:44:39.865
"Stomp on me or smother me.
Do whatever you want."

00:44:39.948 --> 00:44:43.160
"I'll just imagine being under a blanket,
eating tangerines in winter."

00:44:43.994 --> 00:44:45.954
And I just kept still.

00:44:46.538 --> 00:44:47.664
The weird thing was…

00:44:49.875 --> 00:44:52.252
once I started ignoring it,

00:44:52.336 --> 00:44:54.379
it felt like the sleep paralysis
got thrown off.

00:44:54.963 --> 00:44:56.882
I was supposed to be in pain,

00:44:58.133 --> 00:45:00.552
but when I said, "Go ahead, you win"

00:45:01.595 --> 00:45:03.180
and kept still,

00:45:04.097 --> 00:45:05.516
it was almost like it lost steam

00:45:06.225 --> 00:45:09.228
and just slithered away.

00:45:20.030 --> 00:45:22.282
It felt like I learned something.

00:45:24.993 --> 00:45:29.373
Some things are worth a fight,
and some aren't.

00:45:29.456 --> 00:45:32.960
And sleep paralysis
wasn't something worth a fight.

00:45:43.929 --> 00:45:46.265
Don't fight the thing
that's giving you a hard time, Eun-a.

00:45:47.182 --> 00:45:48.350
It's like sleep paralysis.

00:45:49.851 --> 00:45:51.520
If you just ignore it, it'll pass.

00:45:52.646 --> 00:45:53.981
Just let it go on its way.

00:45:59.486 --> 00:46:01.530
I feel better now after talking.

00:46:02.281 --> 00:46:03.782
It's been hard these past few days,

00:46:04.658 --> 00:46:06.952
but this definitely proves
that talking gives me energy.

00:46:10.622 --> 00:46:12.207
What's been giving you a hard time?

00:46:15.168 --> 00:46:19.590
Well, I made it to the final round,
so I went in for the interview, but…

00:46:19.673 --> 00:46:21.425
Damn it, I always make it
to the final round.

00:46:22.175 --> 00:46:23.093
Anyway…

00:46:25.971 --> 00:46:28.473
You can tell the moment
you walk into an interview

00:46:28.557 --> 00:46:30.684
whether you've got it or not.

00:46:31.518 --> 00:46:34.021
I was thinking that I didn't get it again

00:46:34.730 --> 00:46:35.814
and just sat there.

00:46:36.523 --> 00:46:40.736
Then at the last minute,
a judge asked why I wanted to make films.

00:46:42.237 --> 00:46:43.363
She asked, and…

00:46:47.868 --> 00:46:48.702
Well…

00:46:50.245 --> 00:46:52.914
As I was answering, I got choked up.
It was humiliating.

00:46:55.959 --> 00:46:57.127
What did you say?

00:46:58.128 --> 00:46:59.963
Why do you want to make films?

00:47:09.348 --> 00:47:10.182
I want to…

00:47:12.309 --> 00:47:13.810
I want to see someone…

00:47:17.439 --> 00:47:19.316
living on the opposite side of the world…

00:47:29.326 --> 00:47:30.702
and feel that I exist there too.

00:47:37.292 --> 00:47:38.335
I just…

00:47:39.127 --> 00:47:40.754
What gets to me more than losing the grant

00:47:41.630 --> 00:47:43.715
is that I couldn't hold back my tears.

00:47:44.883 --> 00:47:46.718
That's what kills me the most.

00:47:49.262 --> 00:47:52.265
On top of that, I said…

00:47:54.309 --> 00:47:55.310
All for one…

00:47:56.603 --> 00:47:57.437
and one for all.

00:48:00.190 --> 00:48:01.608
I mean, seriously.

00:48:02.484 --> 00:48:05.612
Why did I say,
"All for one, and one for all"?

00:48:05.696 --> 00:48:08.365
What am I going to do? I'm so embarrassed.

00:48:31.763 --> 00:48:33.432
My nose stopped bleeding.

00:49:44.795 --> 00:49:47.589
Why do you have
Director Kim Hyeon-tae's screenplay

00:49:47.672 --> 00:49:49.257
when the producer in charge
hasn't even seen it yet?

00:49:49.883 --> 00:49:53.887
Don't you dare review screenplays
behind my back again.

00:49:56.348 --> 00:49:57.224
Review this.

00:50:18.954 --> 00:50:20.789
If I get choked up while writing,

00:50:22.040 --> 00:50:23.458
the audience will get choked up too.

00:50:23.959 --> 00:50:25.961
If I laugh while writing,

00:50:26.044 --> 00:50:27.629
the audience will laugh too.

00:50:28.421 --> 00:50:31.591
If I feel pain while writing,
the audience will also feel pain.

00:50:33.343 --> 00:50:35.887
Did you get choked up writing this?
Or did you laugh?

00:50:38.765 --> 00:50:41.434
Stringing letters together isn't writing.

00:50:41.518 --> 00:50:43.770
You have to make people feel something.

00:50:43.854 --> 00:50:46.356
When we were little,
we used to walk around like this.

00:50:47.148 --> 00:50:48.275
Do you remember?

00:50:48.358 --> 00:50:49.609
Do you see any adults
walking around like that?

00:50:50.193 --> 00:50:51.319
Are there any adults so happy?

00:50:51.403 --> 00:50:53.029
Nope. There aren't any.

00:50:53.530 --> 00:50:55.574
That's why they go to the movie theater.

00:50:56.700 --> 00:50:57.659
To feel.

00:50:58.410 --> 00:51:00.912
They want to get choked up,
be moved to tears,

00:51:00.996 --> 00:51:02.455
and crack up.

00:51:03.456 --> 00:51:06.418
They want to feel alive again.

00:51:06.501 --> 00:51:09.212
So don't just force a story together
with words.

00:51:09.296 --> 00:51:11.339
Kick the story into gear.

00:51:11.423 --> 00:51:12.757
Bring out people's emotions!

00:51:13.341 --> 00:51:15.594
How do you kick a story into gear?

00:51:19.890 --> 00:51:21.057
Open a thousand doors.

00:51:22.017 --> 00:51:23.768
And make your way through them.

00:51:24.686 --> 00:51:27.063
And the background music should be

00:51:27.689 --> 00:51:28.565
guitar music.

00:52:15.320 --> 00:52:19.407
"It also means facing fear and guilt."

00:52:19.491 --> 00:52:20.617
"Fear…"

00:52:26.790 --> 00:52:27.624
What is it?

00:52:28.708 --> 00:52:29.751
What do you want?

00:52:32.796 --> 00:52:36.716
I've always struggled to deal with people
who walk all over me.

00:52:38.218 --> 00:52:40.178
Should I avoid them,
or put them in their place?

00:52:42.472 --> 00:52:44.349
I always chose to avoid them.

00:52:45.433 --> 00:52:46.393
But this time,

00:52:47.644 --> 00:52:49.229
I'm going to put them in their place.

00:52:51.982 --> 00:52:55.568
I've never once thought you were powerful.

00:52:56.611 --> 00:52:58.363
I do think you're a pain in the ass.

00:52:59.614 --> 00:53:01.282
I hope you don't get those two confused.

00:53:01.783 --> 00:53:02.951
Also,

00:53:03.785 --> 00:53:05.537
I'm a quiet person,

00:53:06.121 --> 00:53:07.664
but I'm not a weak pushover.

00:53:08.581 --> 00:53:10.083
I hope you don't confuse this as well.

00:53:15.797 --> 00:53:19.634
Please don't assume I'm quitting
by pulling some stunt.

00:53:20.260 --> 00:53:21.553
I don't intend to quit.

00:53:33.231 --> 00:53:34.232
It must be entertaining,

00:53:35.233 --> 00:53:37.193
watching someone get pushed out.

00:53:38.486 --> 00:53:39.446
It is entertaining.

00:53:40.155 --> 00:53:42.115
I'll admit it
because I've felt that before too.

00:53:42.824 --> 00:53:43.700
But you know,

00:53:44.325 --> 00:53:46.327
I'd rather you be upfront about it,
like Hwang Dong-man.

00:53:48.038 --> 00:53:51.166
"It's so satisfying to see
that you've lost Mr. Choi's favor."

00:53:53.710 --> 00:53:55.420
At least that'd be amusing.

00:53:57.422 --> 00:53:58.798
What did you just say?

00:54:04.429 --> 00:54:06.473
-Hey, Ax--
-I'm taking off early.

00:54:08.224 --> 00:54:10.769
Or should I stay and endure

00:54:10.852 --> 00:54:12.270
this awkward atmosphere?

00:54:13.063 --> 00:54:14.731
I'm confident I can endure it.

00:54:15.732 --> 00:54:19.736
I've been tied to a desk since I was nine,
so I know I can handle it.

00:54:21.279 --> 00:54:22.947
But can the rest of you handle it?

00:54:46.763 --> 00:54:48.598
Is something contagious going around?

00:54:49.182 --> 00:54:50.600
Why are all these losers acting up?

00:54:53.186 --> 00:54:54.020
Where are you?

00:54:55.146 --> 00:54:56.231
Agit.

00:54:56.314 --> 00:54:57.732
We should meet. Come outside.

00:55:13.373 --> 00:55:14.415
Hey, it's Dong-man.

00:55:28.555 --> 00:55:29.889
So?

00:55:30.765 --> 00:55:33.059
Did you choke down every last word?

00:55:36.896 --> 00:55:37.814
You know,

00:55:38.481 --> 00:55:43.153
reading that out loud was so exhausting
that I ended up with sleep paralysis.

00:55:43.736 --> 00:55:48.491
Every single word
got under my skin and cut so deep,

00:55:49.742 --> 00:55:51.786
it felt like
I was getting tattooed all over.

00:55:54.247 --> 00:55:56.082
Write your screenplays like that!

00:55:56.166 --> 00:55:57.125
You asshole.

00:55:57.208 --> 00:55:58.751
-No, don't!
-Hold on.

00:56:00.920 --> 00:56:02.922
Every word was dripping with sincerity.

00:56:04.007 --> 00:56:06.634
It was the best thing
you've written so far.

00:56:06.718 --> 00:56:07.719
Write your screenplays like that!

00:56:07.802 --> 00:56:08.678
You crazy bastard!

00:56:08.761 --> 00:56:10.138
-Hold on!
-Stop!

00:56:11.556 --> 00:56:13.183
What pisses me off the most

00:56:13.266 --> 00:56:15.310
is you assuming that I'm so miserable.

00:56:15.935 --> 00:56:19.647
Things aren't working out for me,
so I should shut up and be miserable

00:56:19.731 --> 00:56:21.941
and know my place, right?

00:56:22.775 --> 00:56:25.528
Want to hear something really shocking?

00:56:26.446 --> 00:56:27.572
Guess what?

00:56:27.655 --> 00:56:30.950
I'm not as miserable
as you all think I am.

00:56:32.535 --> 00:56:36.247
I bet a pampered rich kid
can't even begin to imagine

00:56:36.331 --> 00:56:38.875
how people can live
in a basement apartment.

00:56:38.958 --> 00:56:41.336
I bet they think they're really miserable.

00:56:41.419 --> 00:56:44.881
Screw that. People who live there
laugh and have fun too.

00:56:44.964 --> 00:56:48.760
They're not pretending.
They really aren't miserable.

00:56:49.385 --> 00:56:50.428
I bet you all thought

00:56:51.054 --> 00:56:53.097
everything would be great
once you debuted.

00:56:53.765 --> 00:56:56.017
You thought it'd be
a whole new world, right?

00:56:56.601 --> 00:56:58.353
So did anything change?

00:56:58.436 --> 00:56:59.270
No, right?

00:56:59.354 --> 00:57:01.564
It's the same.

00:57:01.648 --> 00:57:05.109
After 20 years,
14 screenplays, and no debut,

00:57:05.193 --> 00:57:08.112
I'm just like the rest of you.

00:57:08.821 --> 00:57:11.157
I'm just as miserable

00:57:11.241 --> 00:57:13.576
and just as happy as the rest of you.

00:57:13.660 --> 00:57:17.038
Actually, my life could be
way more fun than yours.

00:57:18.331 --> 00:57:21.793
This is all to say
that you guys are no better than me,

00:57:21.876 --> 00:57:23.503
so stop acting so superior.

00:57:24.879 --> 00:57:28.341
Do you really believe that,
or have you completely lost your mind?

00:57:28.424 --> 00:57:29.551
Also!

00:57:29.634 --> 00:57:32.762
You say I need to talk less,
but I won't ever do that.

00:57:32.845 --> 00:57:35.139
Joking is the only thing
that makes me feel like I exist.

00:57:35.223 --> 00:57:36.683
If I stop talking, I'm dead.

00:57:36.766 --> 00:57:38.351
What's life? It's one long story.

00:57:38.434 --> 00:57:40.228
When the story ends, so does life.

00:57:40.311 --> 00:57:42.564
So don't stop me from making jokes.

00:57:42.647 --> 00:57:45.316
It's the same thing as killing me.

00:57:45.400 --> 00:57:47.819
Even if the world ends tomorrow,

00:57:47.902 --> 00:57:49.445
I'll keep cracking jokes

00:57:49.529 --> 00:57:52.073
because it's the only proof
of my existence!

00:57:52.657 --> 00:57:54.409
What do you keep looking at?

00:58:00.498 --> 00:58:01.457
That's right.

00:58:02.750 --> 00:58:06.796
Your brother said he'll keep making jokes
and talking behind people's backs,

00:58:06.879 --> 00:58:08.089
even if the world ends tomorrow,

00:58:08.172 --> 00:58:11.509
because it's too hard
for him to keep quiet!

00:58:12.093 --> 00:58:15.096
We need to let people
who can't shut the hell up

00:58:15.179 --> 00:58:17.432
run their mouths until they drop dead!

00:58:17.515 --> 00:58:19.601
Your brother says
that's how we should live!

00:58:33.489 --> 00:58:36.200
Hey, call the cops.

00:58:36.784 --> 00:58:37.702
I'll take care of him.

00:58:38.286 --> 00:58:39.537
No objections, right?

00:58:54.719 --> 00:58:55.762
Oh jeez.

00:58:55.845 --> 00:58:58.014
-Hold on.
-Hang on.

00:58:59.015 --> 00:59:00.058
Don't do this.

00:59:03.978 --> 00:59:04.979
Please calm down!

00:59:05.063 --> 00:59:06.272
Get off me!

00:59:07.023 --> 00:59:08.566
Wait, don't hit me!

00:59:10.401 --> 00:59:11.319
Are you okay?

00:59:11.402 --> 00:59:13.571
-Please call the police.
-The police?

00:59:13.655 --> 00:59:15.031
Please hurry.

00:59:36.094 --> 00:59:41.724
Your address is
37, Hyowon 2-gil, Dongro-gu, Seoul.

00:59:43.726 --> 00:59:44.852
Occupation?

00:59:52.735 --> 00:59:53.569
Occupation?

01:00:04.080 --> 01:00:05.164
He's a film director.

01:00:07.709 --> 01:00:08.543
Who are you?

01:00:09.502 --> 01:00:10.795
The producer in charge.

01:00:28.229 --> 01:00:29.939
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:00:48.541 --> 01:00:49.459
The Eight Club?

01:00:50.001 --> 01:00:51.669
Forget it. I'm out.

01:00:51.753 --> 01:00:53.504
That's for you shiny people.

01:00:54.005 --> 01:00:55.381
Doing it alone is exhausting.

01:00:55.965 --> 01:00:57.925
I'll stay by your side and watch you.

01:00:58.676 --> 01:01:01.262
I should be the one swearing, you bastard.

01:01:01.345 --> 01:01:03.973
You stole from someone you shouldn't have.

01:01:04.056 --> 01:01:05.767
You stole from a genius, you bastard.

01:01:05.850 --> 01:01:08.227
She turned out to be closer
than I thought.

01:01:08.728 --> 01:01:10.772
She works at Choi Film.

01:01:11.355 --> 01:01:12.774
-Hi!
-Jang Mi-ran knows me?

01:01:14.150 --> 01:01:16.152
Park Gyeong-se is a bastard
Damn Gyeong-se is a bastard

01:01:16.235 --> 01:01:17.361
Hey, let me ask you something.

01:01:17.445 --> 01:01:19.363
Why have you been so mean to me?

01:01:19.447 --> 01:01:21.073
Because you hated me first.

01:01:22.283 --> 01:01:24.118
What made you hate me so much?

01:01:26.704 --> 01:01:31.709
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim